  "method_semantics": "Official KSH national-accounts employment estimates using LFS-to-national-accounts bridges, administrative records, sole-proprietor registers and exhaustiveness adjustments. Actual hours combine employment and average actual hours from labour reports/LFS. Persons with multiple jobs are assigned to principal activity; market/non-market resident producing units are included. Not directly observed programme effects.",
  "missingness_rule": "Omitted sparse values, explicit null values, numeric zero and status flags are distinct. No supplied status flag means only none supplied. Missing SELF is not inferred zero when EMP equals SAL; missing U remains null even when partial sums equal totals.",
  "within_row_residual_rule": "Report EMP minus SAL minus SELF only for complete source triplets; do not force equality. Persons display residuals up to 0.01 are consistent with independently rounded published values, without a source-provided repair. Zero hour residual is not evidence that skipped cells equal zero.",
  "shared_lineage": "Employment, A10/PE controls, production accounts and IO share KSH_HUNGARIAN_NATIONAL_ACCOUNTS compilation lineage. Agreement is an accounting consistency check, not independent corroboration.",
  "price_unit_bridge": "Current nama_10_a64 CP_MNAC and frozen IO MIO_NAC are both current-price million HUF for 2023. The common unit/year permits difference diagnostics only; it does not establish vintage alignment, labour intensity or a currency/price conversion.",
  "vintage_boundary": "Employment country-specific vintage remains unestablished. Current production accounts differ from frozen IO vintage 2025; vintage compatibility is not established. These are observed accounting-snapshot differences, not employment revision estimates or proof that every difference is exclusively a revision rather than another compilation distinction. Frozen IO is not replaced.",
  "unsupported_claims": [
    "FTE or invented full-time-hours denominator",
    "persons/output or hours/output labour coefficients",
    "reverse employment allocation to 89 IO leaves",
    "complete 64-industry employment closure from partial observed sums",
    "heat-pump installer, occupation cohort or spare capacity",
    "jobs created, net jobs, programme shock, multiplier or inverse",
    "programme GDP, fiscal effects, financing or national deployment defaults",
    "current country-specific employment vintage inferred from global update",
    "B15 readiness, B12 expansion or full B16-D01/B16 acceptance"
  ],
